<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Fertile Fields' compost chain accepts manure.

    MakeCompost and MakeCompost5 are "make raw compost from organic waste", already taking hay,
    plant scraps, rotted mush, kibble and pemmican, measured by mass through
    RFF_Code.IngredientValueGetter_Mass. Manure in either state belongs in that list.

    Both are base Fertile Fields defs in Defs/Recipes_RFF.xml, not patch-created, so they exist
    whenever Fertile Fields is loaded. Each operation is still conditional on its own target: a
    PatchOperationSequence stops at the first operation that fails rather than skipping it, so one
    def going away would silence every later one. Separate operations mean one loss costs one
    integration.

    DELIBERATELY NOT PATCHED - Make_FertilizerFromBiosolids and its bulk variant. Adding dry manure
    straight into the biosolids-to-fertilizer recipe would route manure to fertilizer without ever
    passing through a composter, which is the one thing this mod exists to add. The route is
    manure -> composter -> biosolids -> Fertile Fields' fertilizer, and it stays that way.

    ALSO NOT PATCHED - Make_Ash2 and Make_Ash12. Velcroboy's Manure fed manure into them, but they
    are gone from Fertile Fields 1.6: they survive in the mod's 1 through 1.5 folders and appear
    nowhere in 1.6/Patches/PatchesOtherMods.xml. Nothing left to hook.

    Nothing here needs VGP Garden Tools. The original mod's VGP dependency existed only to fix the
    dirt defName in its own fertilizer recipes, which this mod does not carry.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/RecipeDef[defName="MakeCompost" or defName="MakeCompost5"]/ingredients/li/filter/thingDefs</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/RecipeDef[defName="MakeCompost" or defName="MakeCompost5"]/ingredients/li/filter/thingDefs</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>Manure</li>
        <li>DryManure</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/RecipeDef[defName="MakeCompost" or defName="MakeCompost5"]/fixedIngredientFilter/thingDefs</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/RecipeDef[defName="MakeCompost" or defName="MakeCompost5"]/fixedIngredientFilter/thingDefs</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>Manure</li>
        <li>DryManure</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!--
    defaultIngredientFilter is what a new bill starts with ticked. Dry manure is offered by
    default because a colony accumulates it whether or not it wants to; fresh manure is left
    unticked so a bill does not quietly compete with the composter for the same input.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/RecipeDef[defName="MakeCompost" or defName="MakeCompost5"]/defaultIngredientFilter/thingDefs</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/RecipeDef[defName="MakeCompost" or defName="MakeCompost5"]/defaultIngredientFilter/thingDefs</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>DryManure</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
